    "collapsible_content_L7xWEY": {
      "type": "collapsible-content",
      "blocks": {
        "collapsible_row_9qmYYT": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Is it essential to prime the Carbon Cartridges?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Priming the Carbon Cartridges is the first step to ensuring your cartridges are completely free of any residuals from the manufacturing process. The residuals are completely normal and safe but can lead to cloudy water if the cartridges are not correctly primed. We recommend priming your Carbon Cartridges for at least three minutes. If not primed sufficiently, the first four rounds of filtered water may have cloudy white particles that can be safely discarded. NB: The recommended number of priming rounds depends on the type of cart you have. For full priming instructions, <a href=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0735/1821/9557/files/Phoenix_Gravity___Carbon_Filter.pdf\">Download priming instructions (PDF)</a></p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_CyeL7B": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Why is my water cloudy?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Don’t worry, cloudy water after initial installation is normal and completely harmless. It’s simply safe residual dust from the manufacturing process. It can occur if the cartridges are not correctly primed - and we recommend priming cartridges fully (see above). If it is not primed, it can take about four rounds of filtered water to clear.   <br/>please refer to our instruction manual sheet <a href=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0735/1821/9557/files/Phoenix_Gravity___Carbon_Filter.pdf\">instruction manual sheet .</a></p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_zHhNKn": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How long will my Carbon Cartridges last?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>We recommend replacing your Carbon Cartridges every 12 months . The lifespan of a pair of Phoenix Gravity Carbon Cartridges is about 20,000 litres. If you want to subscribe to have your filters replaced, you can do so here.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_cYcBGQ": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How long will the POSTreat Fluoride Removal filters last?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Our POSTreat Filter Cartridges are made from 304-Stainless Steel and are designed to last for years - which is why we include a 10 year warranty with our products. The media inside our proprietary FluoRid media will last for 4000 litres and needs replacing approximately every 4 months. We also offer a subscription service for replacement media - we’ll remember when they’re due, so you don’t have to. To replace your FluoRid media, please visit our  <a href=\"https://phoenixwaterfilters.co.uk/products/postreat-fluorid-media-refill\">POSTreat FluoRid Media Refill</a></p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_DBEKcc": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How long will the FluoRid Media in the POSTreat last?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>The lifespan of a pair of POSTreat Fluoride Removal filters are upto 4,000 Litres. It is recommended to replace the media with \"FluoRid Media Refill\" every 4 months.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_FDF7CG": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Will I be able to assemble my system and change my cartridges myself?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Certainly! Our systems are designed to be extremely easy to assemble and everything you need will be included. You can do it yourself with just your hands - there’s no specialist tools, plumbers or electricians required. We include full instructions with every unit and we’re always here to help. You can <a href=\"/pages/contact\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"New Contact Us\">contact us here.</a></p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_drEUWk": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "My Phoenix Gravity Water Filter has water dripping between the Upper and Lower Chambers. What does this mean?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>This will be from over-filling the Water Filter System. Careful use can help prevent overfilling by checking how much water is in the lower chamber before filling the upper chamber. Once you get to know your usage rates the re-filling process will become second nature! We also sell a vision tap which will enable you to see the water level from the outside.<a href=\"/products/vision-tap-stainless-steel\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Vision Tap- Stainless Steel\"> </a>Please visit our <a href=\"/products/vision-tap-stainless-steel\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Vision Tap- Stainless Steel\">Vision Tap page</a> for more information .</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_Vx6Qmw": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How frequently do I need to change my cartridges?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>This depends on the usage frequency and quality of your water input. As a guide, we recommend replacing them at the following milestones: Carbon Cartridges: 12 months / 20,000 litres. POSTreat (and FluoRid Media Refill): 4 months. We also provide a subscription service that offers a specific percentage discount on every order. Let us remember when you need to change your cartridge, so you don’t have to! For full information, <a href=\"https://phoenixwaterfilters.co.uk/products/the-phoenix-gravity-water-filter\">Visit our Shop.</a></p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_EKwjKN": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How is our Stainless - steel  different?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>It’s made from premium AISI 304 stainless steel, known for its durability, rust resistance, and long-lasting performance. The 8K finish adds a sleek, polished look while keeping the system naturally BPA-free, non-leaching, and built to withstand everyday home and outdoor use.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_ef4BRb": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Are the filter cartridges made of plastic? Is the filter system made of any plastic elements?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Our filter housings are constructed from durable and safe 304-grade stainless steel. The carbon cartridges are made from CTC-60 coconut shell activated carbon and are encased in Noryl, a food-grade material that is free of BPA. This combination ensures the highest quality and safety standards for your drinking water.  </p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        }
      },
