    "collapsible_content_TUC6pH": {
      "type": "collapsible-content",
      "blocks": {
        "collapsible_row_GW8rJj": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How do Phoenix Gravity filters work?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>We use the highest grade 304 stainless steel, natural coconut carbon and other natural materials. Plus the mighty force of gravity! Our advanced filtration system removes up to 99.99% of commonly occurring contaminants and retains up to 100% of minerals. <a href=\"/pages/our-technology\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Our Technology\">Visit our Technology page</a>  to learn more about how it works.<br/><br/></p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_BFMzGy": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What are the carbon cartridges made of?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Our KoKo Carb cartridges are made with CTC60 Grade activated carbon, helping remove both physical and chemical contaminants from your water</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_7x6WWW": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What do your filters really remove?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Phoenix Gravity Carbon filters are made from pure coconut shells, which are a sustainable and a renewable resource. The carbon in the filters are activated, which means that it has a high surface area and is very porous. This allows them to trap a wide range of contaminants, including chlorine, heavy metals, and other impurities. Phoenix Gravity Carbon cartridges are designed to provide clean, odorless water with a great taste. They do not release any harmful chemicals or by-products into the water, and they are super effective at removing chlorine and other volatile organic compounds A pair of carbon cartridges can filter up to 20,000 litres of water by providing safe and healthy drinking water.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_k8pr4r": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How do the carbon cartridges work?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Our KokoCarb Cartridges sit in a gravity-fed filtration process where water naturally passes through them. The dense porous wall captures physical contaminants like sediments, bacteria, cysts, and microplastics, while the silver-impregnated activated carbon helps reduce chemical contaminants such as chlorine, PFAS, and pesticides.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_YqdXBf": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Do Phoenix Gravity Filters remove residual pharmaceutical waste?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Yes, up to 99.99%! Our primary Smart Carbon Cartridges have been independently tested for many Volatile Organic compounds including 1,4- dichlorobenzene, 2-Butanone, Acetone, Allyl Chloride and many more. For full test results, please visit our <a href=\"/pages/get-help\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"New Get Help\">Help Centre </a></p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_BTFxHp": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Do the Phoenix Carbon Cartridges remove fluoride?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>They certainly can! We’ve designed a specialist fluoride cartridge called the POSTreat to remove over 95% of fluoride from your tap water. Made from the highest grade stainless steel, it’s completely reusable and refillable, with our POSTreat FluoRid Refill. The POSTreat can be used in conjunction with primary Carbon Cartridges. For full details or to buy the POSTreat,  <br/>please visit the <a href=\"/products/postreat-fluoride-remover\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"POSTreat Fluoride Removal Filter Cartridge\">POSTreat page</a> Looking for a refill? Please visit the <a href=\"/products/postreat-fluorid-media-refill\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"POSTreat FluoRid Media Refill\">FluoRid Refill page.</a></p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_MbNLHd": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Do Phoenix Carbon Cartridges eliminate phthalates from water?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>While we have not specifically tested for the removal of phthalates, our Phoenix Carbon Cartridges are made with highest grade activated coconut carbon, which is known for its effectiveness in adsorbing phthalates from water. We are constantly improving and testing our filters. Find the full list of what we remove on our  <a href=\"https://phoenixwaterfilters.co.uk/pages/help-center\">Help Centre</a></p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_WPwjUH": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Do Phoenix Gravity filters remove Estrogen?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>While we have not specifically tested for the removal of estrogen, our Phoenix Carbon Filters are made with activated coconut carbon, which is known for its effectiveness in adsorbing estrogen from water. We are constantly improving and testing our filters. Find the full list of what we in our <a href=\"/pages/get-help\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"New Get Help\">Help Centre.</a> Additionally, supporting research is available on PubMed.<a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/22123241/?utm_source=chatgpt.com\" target=\"_blank\">PubMed study on estrogen </a></p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_aaHCi7": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Can it filter PFAS and pesticides?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>The activated carbon uses adsorption technology to help reduce PFAS, pesticides, and other chemical contaminants by more than 99.66% from your water.<br/><br/></p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_ARRB7k": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How do Phoenix Gravity  Filters and cartridges compare to others?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>We are one of the leaders in advanced Gravity Filtration. With over 40 years’ experience of manufacturing in-house, we have complete control over the process and the quality of our filters and cartridges. We are enormously proud of the effort it has taken us to become a leading manufacturer of Gravity Water Filters.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_Un8MXb": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Are Phoenix Gravity filters as comprehensive as Berkey?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Absolutely! We have run extensive and independent tests on our filters for a variety of microbiological contaminants such as e-coli bacteria, MS2 Phage viruses and chemical contaminants such as Lead, chlorine, chromium, Volatile organic compounds and 100 more. What’s more, with over 40 years’ experience of in-house manufacturing - we’re one of the leading global manufacturers of stainless steel gravity filtration systems. We also have complete control over the process and the quality of our filters and cartridges. We are enormously proud of the effort it has taken us to become the world’s leading manufacturer of Gravity Water Filters. For more details, <a href=\"https://phoenixwaterfilters.co.uk/\">click here.</a></p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_qcnCFw": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Do Phoenix Gravity Filters lower the TDS?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>TDS stands for Total Dissolved Solids and is measured in parts per million (ppm) or parts per billion (ppb). It’s a measure of the water’s organic and inorganic content including minerals. Natural water will have a TDS reading from minerals picked up from the rocks and ground it flows through. It’s generally accepted that 300 ppm is a good mineral content. We purposely do not bring our TDS to zero, because we’re all about preserving the minerals your body needs.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_b6mKGe": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Will Phoenix Gravity Filters remove water hardness?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>No. Phoenix Carbon Filter Cartridges are designed to remove up to 99.99% of bacteria, viruses, chlorine, lead and over 100 other unwanted substances from your drinking water. However, it’s important to note Phoenix Gravity Water Filters are not designed to lower water hardness. In fact, many of the natural minerals that make the water hard are essential to good health- we want to retain as many as possible! Hardness (and TDS) is measured in ppm, it’s generally accepted that 300 ppm is a good mineral content of water. For more details on what we remove, please visit our <a href=\"/pages/get-help\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"New Get Help\">Help Centre</a>.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_FdL48L": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What is the fluoride filter made of?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>The filter is housed in high-quality 304 stainless steel, a safe and chemically neutral material designed for durable everyday water filtration.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_AyW8pX": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Do your filters remove arsenic from water?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Yes, Phoenix Gravity filter systems can help reduce arsenic in water. For the most effective results, we recommend using our KokoCarb Cartridges together with the POSTreat Fluoride Removal Filter Cartridge.This combination works very effectively in addressing contaminants such as arsenic and fluoride, and has been shown to remove over 99.9% of arsenic & over 95% of fluoride when used correctly.Many customers who rely on borehole or well water sources choose this combination for improved water quality and safety.You can review more details about the<a href=\"https://phoenixwaterfilters.co.uk/products/postreat-fluoride-remover?selling_plan=710193840512&variant=49561020760357\" title=\"https://phoenixwaterfilters.co.uk/products/postreat-fluoride-remover?selling_plan=710193840512&variant=49561020760357\"> filter cartridge here</a></p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_XNH9w9": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Does it remove hormones and pharmaceutical residues from water?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Our Phoenix Gravity Water Filter uses activated carbon to effectively reduce hormones such as Oestrogen, along with other pharmaceutical-related contaminants and harmful substances from your drinking water.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_DUmUMQ": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What certifications do Phoenix Gravity Water Filters have, and which products do they apply to?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Phoenix Gravity Water Filters are independently certified to NSF/ANSI 42, 372, and 401 standards, covering contaminant reduction, material safety, and emerging contaminants such as PFAS and microplastics. These certifications apply to the Phoenix Gravity Water Filter systems and relevant filtration components.</p><p>Carbon Cartridges - NSF/ANSI 42 (safely reduces non-health-related contaminants that impact the taste, odor, or visual appearance of water such as chlorine, particulates and iron) </p><p>Filter System - NSF/ANSI 42 (safely reduces non-health-related contaminants that impact the taste, odor, or visual appearance of water such as chlorine, particulates and iron) & NSF/ANSI/CAN 372 (standard that establishes testing methods and verification procedures for the \"lead-free\" content of drinking water system components) </p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_feH73C": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Which Phoenix products are third-party tested and under what standards?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>The Phoenix Gravity Water Systems and KokoCarb Cartridges are independently tested and verified by accredited third-party laboratories under NSF/WQA standards to ensure performance, safety, and filtration effectiveness.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_jDGqhP": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Are there any natural vitamins and minerals left after the filtration process ?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Yes, our gravity filtration system is designed to retain many of the beneficial naturally occurring minerals in water, such as calcium, magnesium, and potassium, while reducing unwanted contaminants like chlorine, heavy metals, sediment, and other impurities. The filtration process focuses on improving water quality and taste while still preserving the healthy mineral balance naturally present in the water. </p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_G6FCYL": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Does it remove chloramine ?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Yes, Phoenix Gravity Filters are designed to effectively reduce chloramine from water. The activated carbon filtration media helps remove up to 99.9% of chloramine, along with chlorine, bad tastes, odors, and other common contaminants, while still retaining beneficial natural minerals.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_UUxVBL": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": " Does Phoenix Gravity water filters remove limescale ?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p><br/>Our filters do not remove limescale, as it is primarily made up of calcium and magnesium, which are essential minerals that your body needs.</p><p>Our system is specifically designed to remove harmful contaminants while retaining beneficial minerals like these. As a result, a small amount of limescale is completely normal and does not affect the quality or safety of your filtered water. (possibly mention TDS?)</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_cR8bJt": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "I have a different stand alone system. Can I use Phoenix Gravity cartridges with them ?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Yes, our Phoenix Gravity KokoCarb Cartridges are compatible with most stand-alone gravity-fed water filtration systems. They are designed for easy installation and reliable filtration performance across similar gravity filtration units. </p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_JqDRif": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Are these Phoenix Gravity cartridges compatible with the Berkey system?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Yes, our Phoenix Gravity KokoCarb Cartridges are fully compatible with Berkey water filter systems. They are designed to fit seamlessly into compatible gravity-fed systems while providing reliable and effective filtration performance</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_D6Xz4y": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Does the TDS value change after the filtration is done?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Yes, the TDS value may change slightly after filtration, but Phoenix Gravity Water Filters are designed to remove unwanted impurities while retaining beneficial natural minerals like calcium and magnesium. Forget the myth that zero TDS means perfect water; ideal drinking water typically falls within 100–500 ppm TDS, as these dissolved minerals are important for healthy, great-tasting water.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        }
      },
